        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "[codex] Keep split WebVNC responsive",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- route outbound WebVNC agent sockets through an optional exact-origin agent URL while keeping coordinator APIs on the coordinator origin\n- keep framebuffer and heartbeat handling responsive while theme updates run asynchronously\n- fully detach long-lived Wayland wallpaper processes from their launching SSH sessions\n- expose the effective agent URL through JSON config diagnostics and document the deployment boundary\n\n## Root cause\n\nSplit-origin deployments reused one coordinator URL for both coordinator APIs and outbound agent sockets. Theme application also ran synchronously on the bootstrap message path, while the Wayland wallpaper process retained SSH session state. Together these could leave an authenticated viewer connected to a blank canvas or stall updates during theme work.\n\n## Impact\n\nOperators can route the agent socket to a separate trusted origin without forwarding coordinator credentials. Viewers continue receiving framebuffer and heartbeat traffic during theme changes, and the wallpaper survives the bootstrap SSH session cleanly.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Go race tests for CLI and local-container packages\n- worker formatting and TypeScript checks\n- 17 focused worker bootstrap tests\n- guarded split-origin live WebVNC E2E held one daemon and bridge connection stable for 100 seconds while applying fresh themes\n",
